## Reproducer

```
CUDA_PATH=/usr/local/cuda CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$HOME/work/zen/jxl-encoder-shared-target \
  cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder --example w44_phase3_b4_gpu_linear_planes_ab \
  --features "gpu-butteraugli butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop parallel __expert"
```

## Follow-on candidates (NOT in B4 scope)

1. **Default-on flip for `gpu-butteraugli`** — now structurally viable.
   The B4 measurement (11-21% wall reduction, zero regressions) is
   strong enough to justify making the GPU backend the default when
   the cargo feature is enabled. Needs a separate chunk that wires
   defaults + adds an opt-out.
2. **Persistent GPU recon-plane handles** — the encoder allocates
   fresh GPU buffers for each iter's distorted-side upload (3
   `create_from_slice` calls / iter). If the buttloop is rewired to
   keep recon planes resident on the GPU across iters, we can avoid
   the host→GPU upload entirely on the distorted side. Probably saves
   another 5-10% wall at 1 MP.
3. **GPU multi-resolution end-to-end** — buttloop's per-tile distance
   computation is still on CPU after the GPU returns the diffmap.
   Pushing that to GPU would shave ~10-30 ms / iter at large sizes.
4. **Cell coverage expansion** — extend to 30+ cells across 256²,
   512², 1024², 2048², 4096² × distances {0.5, 1, 2, 4, 8} now that
   the integration is proven on the 6-cell harness.

## DO NOT (binding for future agents)

- DO NOT remove the dead-code LUT entirely without first confirming
  no future regression resurrects the sRGB-u8 path. The
  `#[allow(dead_code)]` is intentional documentation.
- DO NOT enable `gpu-butteraugli` by default in CI matrices that
  don't run on a CUDA host — the cargo feature triggers a CubeCL +
  CUDA compile which takes 5-9 min cold even when no GPU is present.
- DO NOT cite "FMA precision" for the 0.225% byte delta on
  cid22_1418519_e8_d2 (per W44-66 user correction). The drift is the
  buttloop landing on a slightly different convergence point because
  the GPU's reduction tree order produces a marginally different
  butteraugli score (~1e-7 relative) which moves the gradient
  descent direction by a hair.
- DO NOT raise `TIME_ITERS` past 4 without rotating cells — at 4
  iters this bench takes ~80 s; at 8 iters it would take 160 s.
  Per-iter variance is small enough at 4 that more iters won't move
  the means.
